    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0797ae30",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: i'm just here for the boobs; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a movie theater looking directly at the camera with a smirk while holding popcorn, with the text overlay \"i'm just here for the boobs\". The scene is set in a dark theater with other audience members visible, some of whom are also watching the screen or engaged in their own activities. The overall intent of the meme is to humorously or sarcastically suggest that the man is only there for the physical appearance of the actors or actresses in the movie, specifically focusing on their breasts. This intent is rooted in objectification and reduces the value of the cinematic experience to a sexualized focus on body parts, which aligns with misogynistic tropes that objectify women based on their physical attributes. The meme uses the juxtaposition of the man's casual, self-aware expression with the explicit text to convey a tone of ironic detachment from the film's content, while simultaneously reinforcing the idea that women's bodies are the primary attraction in media. This is a clear example of mysogynous content as it centers on the sexualization of women's bodies and implies that their value lies in their physical appearance, particularly their breasts, rather than their talent, character, or contribution to the film.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_726e3adb"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
